# a program that looks like it counts forever. it does not produce anything.
#
# `count(N + 1)` is not bigger than `count(N)`: the arithmetic folds straight
# back to a single number, so the term never grows and there is nothing to
# watch. the checker says so before you run it.
#
# compare nats.kudzu, where the rule hands a number to the term on its way
# past. one character of difference, and it is the whole language.

count(N) => count(N + 1)

seed count(0)
